 turnIndex`, and derived views by `processId, updatedAt`. Fastify routes expose cursor pagination and default page limits. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:78:The design is deliberately conservative around derived views. Turns and\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:80:archive entries. A derived turn or chunk candidate can be rebuilt from the\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:147:| Turn references must stay stable across rebuilds | Derived views cannot dangle when turn cache is refreshed | Turns get deterministic `turnId` values and derived views store stable turn ids plus turn-index ranges, not Convex row ids |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:148:| Derived views are structural only | Prevents scope creep into summarization | `turn_range` and `chunk_candidate` contain boundaries/provenance, not generated summaries |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:212:| `convex/derivedArchiveViews.ts` | New | Store/read structural derived views | Convex schema | AC-5.x, AC-7.x |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:244:  bodyText: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:308:  viewKind: v.union(v.literal('turn_range'), v.literal('chunk_candidate')),\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:314:  bodyText: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:327:For `turn_range`, `startTurnIndex` and `endTurnIndex` are required by Fastify\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:328:validation before persistence. For `chunk_candidate`, the view must include\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:330:summary content. Derived-view rows may be deleted and recreated from turns; this\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:334:bounded. Epic 7 limits turn rows to one process turn and derived views to small\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:362:  bodyText: string | null;\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:392:  viewKind: 'turn_range' | 'chunk_candidate';\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:397:  bodyText: string | null;\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:454:    bodyText?: string | null;\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:517:    bodyText?: string | null;\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:641:- `turn_range`: one contiguous range of turn indexes with source entry ids\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:642:- `chunk_candidate`: a candidate grouping over one or more turns for future\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:645:Neither view contains model-generated summaries. `bodyText`, when present, is a\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:674:- derived views: default 50\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:689:| 5 | Structural derived views | `turn_range`, `chunk_candidate`, refresh, degradation | AC-5.x | Relevant sections: Flow 5, Route Validation. Non-TC: no generated summary body, stale/rebuilt derived views |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:724:- [x] Turns and derived views are rebuildable, not canonical.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:97:| A5 | Chunk and summary strategies may vary by process type later | Validated | Platform | Epic 7 establishes a non-summarizing structural derived-view foundation without hard-coding a universal summarizer |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:319:In Epic 7, a derived view is a non-summarizing structural projection over one or\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:322:require or create model-generated summary content.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:327:2. System creates or returns a structural derived view over one or more turns\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:328:3. User or process reads the derived view\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:329:4. The derived view links back to the source turns and archive entries\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:330:5. Later derived views can be rebuilt without changing the archive\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:334:**AC-5.1:** The platform can expose a non-summarizing structural derived view\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:339:  - When: User requests a derived view\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:340:  - Then: The platform returns a derived view that identifies the turn boundary\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:341:    and does not require generated summary text\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:347:  - Given: A derived view is returned for a turn range\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:355:  - Given: A derived view is returned\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:359:  - Given: A derived view references turns\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:365:- **TC-5.4a: Archive remains after derived view creation**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:366:  - Given: A derived view has been created or refreshed\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:377:  - Given: A derived view cannot fully resolve source turns or metadata\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:423:Archive and derived views must remain usable across reloads, process pauses,\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:441:  - Given: A derived view exists for a process\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:443:  - Then: The derived view remains readable or can be rebuilt from turns\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:481:| Refresh derived archive views | POST | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/archive/derived-views/refresh` | Requests rebuild or refresh of derived views from canonical turns |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:495:| bodyText | string | no | non-empty when present | Human-readable body for text-like entries |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:544:| viewKind | enum | yes | `turn_range` or `chunk_candidate` | Kind of structural derived view in this first slice |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:545:| turnRange.startIndex | integer | no | required for `turn_range`; non-negative when present | First covered turn index for range-based views |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:546:| turnRange.endIndex | integer | no | required for `turn_range`; greater than or equal to `startIndex` when present | Last covered turn index for range-based views |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:550:| bodyText | string | no | non-empty when present | Optional non-generated structural note or label content; model-generated summary content is out of scope |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:551:| viewStatus | enum | yes | `ready` or `degraded` | Whether the derived view resolved cleanly |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:552:| degradationReason | string | no | non-empty when present | Why the derived view 