{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_108","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"The archive primitive, turn derivation, and derived-view layers are implemented against the full Epic 7 taxonomy, but the live execution/finalization path still feeds them legacy `ProcessHistoryItem` data, so later stories are validated against seeded archive rows instead of the real runtime source.\",\"Story 6 provenance enrichment is disconnected from Stories 2-3 production writes: archive reads can enrich `relatedArtifactVersionId` and `relatedSourceProvenanceId`, but the shipped append paths never persist those IDs.\",\"The archive page, turn page, and derived-view page all work when archive rows already exist, but the default shipped execution flow does not generate the archive shape those stories were designed around.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"`ExecutionResult` is still typed as `processHistoryItems: ProcessHistoryItem[]`, and `ProcessHistoryItem` still exposes the legacy presentation vocabulary rather than the canonical archive taxonomy.\",\"The design contract said archive rows would store nullable artifact/source/tool IDs and read services would enrich later; current checkpoint/provenance interfaces do not return the identifiers needed to realize that contract on the live path.\",\"The process work-surface contract/UI never added the designed archive entry point, so archive/turn/view routes are not connected to the primary process surface.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"`corepack pnpm run green-verify` and `corepack pnpm run verify-all` both exited 0.\",\"Automation is masking the main integration gaps: tests such as `tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts` and `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` seed canonical archive rows directly, and `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` seeds provenance-linked rows directly, instead of proving the live runtime can emit them.\",\"The gate is still lighter than the epic implies: `guard:no-test-changes` prints `SKIP` and `test:e2e` is scaffold-only, so there is no executable end-to-end check for live archive generation or archive navigation.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"`createApp` wires `new ScriptExecutionService(providerAdapterRegistry)` by default, and that service still uses the documented Epic 3 default placeholder payload; the placeholder emits a synthetic `process_event` plus \\\"Execution placeholder...\\\" side-work output rather than real low-level archive material.\",\"No production archive append path populates `relatedArtifactVersionId`, `relatedSourceProvenanceId`, or `relatedToolCallId`; the live appenders explicitly write those fields as `null`, so provenance and tool-correlation behavior is unreachable from real traffic.\",\"Checkpoint persistence and source-provenance recording happen only after archive finalization and expose no archive-linkable identifiers back to the archive writer, so Story 6 enrichment currently works only for pre-seeded/test-fixture rows.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-E7-001\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"title\":\"Live execution cannot emit the Epic 7 archive taxonomy\",\"evidence\":\"`ProcessHistoryItem` only allows `user_message|process_message|progress_update|attention_request|side_work_update|process_event` in `apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts:124-131`, and `ExecutionResult` still exposes `processHistoryItems: ProcessHistoryItem[]` in `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter.ts:125-132`. `ProcessHistoryCompatService` only maps `user_message`, `process_message`, and `process_event` into archive kinds in `apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts:8-23`. On the shipped path, `createApp` defaults to `new ScriptExecutionService(providerAdapterRegistry)` in `apps/platform/server/app.ts:285-286`, and that default service still uses the documented Epic 3 placeholder payload in `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts:159-177`, which emits only a synthetic `process_event` in `script-execution.service.ts:85-128`. As a result, the runtime cannot produce `reasoning`, `script_emission`, `tool_call`, or `tool_result` archive entries at all, and does not produce real `model_message` traffic without a non-default injected runner.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/app.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"AC-1.2\",\"AC-2.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-E7-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Archive rows never capture artifact/source provenance on the live path\",\"evidence\":\"Both live archive appenders hardcode relation fields to `null`: `apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts:39-56` and `apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:151-167`. During execution, archive finalization happens before provenance recording in `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:563-581` and `690-706`; later checkpoint/provenance steps run separately in `process-environment.service.ts:829-882`. Those downstream interfaces do not return linkable identifiers: `persistCheckpointArtifacts` returns only `PlatformProcessOutputSummary[]` in `apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:386-389`, and `SourceProvenanceService.recordInformedWorkForCurrentSources` / `recordReceivedCodeUpdates` both return `Promise<void>` in `apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts:22-34`. The read-time enrichment added for Story 6 therefore depends on IDs that production never writes.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.4\",\"AC-6.1\",\"AC-6.2\",\"AC-6.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-E7-003\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Process work surface never exposes an archive entry point\",\"evidence\":\"`renderProcessWorkSurfacePage` accepts callbacks for project, review, start, resume, rehydrate, rebuild, and respond only in `apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-work-surface-page.ts:27-45`, and its control switch has no archive navigation case in `process-work-surface-page.ts:140-169`. The shared control contract likewise only defines `start`, `respond`, `resume`, `rehydrate`, `rebuild`, `review`, and `restart` in `apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts:176-206`. The archive route exists, but it is not discoverable from the primary process surface.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-work-surface-page.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"BROWSER-ROUTE-CONTRACT\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"`verify-all` passed, but `test:e2e` is scaffold-only and `guard:no-test-changes` is not implemented, so those gate layers remain unproven.\",\"This review did not manually run `pnpm run convex:dev` and `pnpm dev` to validate archive generation against a live backend/provider session.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}"}}
