{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_99","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"The route, store, client, and test surfaces for archive/turn/view reads are wired end to end, and both `corepack pnpm run green-verify` and `corepack pnpm run verify-all` passed.\",\"Cross-story drift remains between the Story 1/2 write path and the Story 4/5/6 read path: turns, derived views, and provenance enrichment assume a richer canonical archive than the shipped execution path actually produces.\",\"Most low-level archive taxonomy and provenance scenarios are proven with fixtures/in-memory stores rather than by the real execution pipeline.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"The tech design says Fastify should finalize completed model/runtime objects, script emissions, and tool call/result pairs into canonical archive entries, but the implementation still canonicalizes runtime output through presentation-level `processHistoryItems` compatibility mapping.\",\"The design says `archiveTurns` are cached projections for bounded reads, but turn and derived-view GETs rebuild from full archive scans on each request instead of serving cached projections first.\",\"The design expects archive entries to carry nullable artifact/source/tool foreign keys for read-time enrichment, but the shipped writers persist provenance on parallel tables without linking those ids back onto archive rows.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Story 3-5 read surfaces are present and exercised by tests, including access control, empty states, degraded rendering, and derived-view conflict handling.\",\"Story 1-2 are only partially realized on the production path: canonical append currently reaches `user_message`, `model_message`, and `process_event`, not the full seven-kind archive taxonomy required by the epic.\",\"Story 6 provenance coherence is implemented as a read-time enrichment layer, but the write path never supplies the archive-side ids that would let real archive entries surface artifact/source provenance.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"The default execution path still runs the explicit placeholder script payload in `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts`, and that payload emits a single finalized `process_event` instead of real low-level reasoning/script/tool archive objects.\",\"Artifact checkpoints and source-provenance records are persisted on side channels, but the shipped archive writers never attach `relatedArtifactVersionId` or `relatedSourceProvenanceId` to canonical archive entries.\",\"Archive source-provenance enrichment only looks at the newest 200 provenance rows for a process, so older archive pages can report healthy links as degraded once real archive rows start linking to older provenance ids.\",\"Turn and derived-view reads currently pay full-archive rebuild cost on every request rather than using cached projections as the primary bounded read path.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-07-001\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"title\":\"The shipped archive write path never produces four of the seven required canonical entry kinds\",\"evidence\":\"`ExecutionResult` only carries `processHistoryItems`, outputs, side-work writes, and checkpoint candidates (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter.ts:125-132`). `processHistoryItemKindSchema` is limited to `user_message`, `process_message`, `progress_update`, `attention_request`, `side_work_update`, and `process_event` (`apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts:124-131`). Runtime execution stores those history items and then archives them through `appendFromProcessHistoryItem` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:690-706`), while `ProcessHistoryCompatService` only maps `user_message`, `process_message`, and `process_event` into archive entries and hard-codes the related ids to `null` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts:8-12`, `:39-56`). The default production script payload is still the shared placeholder and only emits a finalized `process_event` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts:15-135`, `:158-163`). As shipped, the real path never emits `reasoning`, `script_emission`, `tool_call`, or `tool_result` archive entries.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"AC-1.2\",\"AC-2.3\",\"AC-4.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-07-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Archive provenance coherence is unreachable on the real write path because archive rows never record related artifact/source ids\",\"evidence\":\"Accepted user-response archiving explicitly writes `relatedArtifactVersionId: null` and `relatedSourceProvenanceId: null` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:151-167`). The compatibility archive path also hard-codes all related ids to `null` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts:39-56`). Meanwhile the execution/checkpoint flow persists artifacts and source provenance on separate paths via `persistCheckpointArtifacts`, `recordInformedWorkForCurrentSources`, and `recordReceivedCodeUpdates` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:577-581`, `:830-883`), and `SourceProvenanceService` creates durable provenance rows separately (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts:200-218`). Because no shipped archive writer threads those ids back onto archive entries, the Story 6 enrichment surface is only reachable from fixtures/tests, not from real archive data.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.4\",\"AC-6.1\",\"AC-6.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-07-003\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Source provenance enrichment can falsely degrade older archive entries because it only loads the newest 200 provenance rows\",\"evidence\":\"`listProcessSourceProvenanceEntries` returns only the 200 most recent source-provenance records for a process (`convex/sourceProvenance.ts:58-71`). `ArchiveReadService` loads that process-wide slice once when any page contains `relatedSourceProvenanceId` values (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts:120-126`) and resolves each entry from that in-memory map (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts:148-160`). If an archive page references an older but still-existing provenance id outside the newest 200 rows, the entry is incorrectly degraded with `Related source provenance is unavailable.` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts:198-200`).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"convex/sourceProvenance.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.4\",\"AC-6.2\",\"AC-6.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"EV-07-004\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Turn and derived-view reads bypass the cached-projection design and rescan the full archive on every request\",\"evidence\":\"`getTurns` always calls `rebuildTurns` before reading a page (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts:61-85`), and `rebuildTurns` paginates through the entire archive (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts:89-110`). `listViews` and `refreshViews` likewise rebuild turns and recompute full-archive signatures by scanning all archive entries before responding (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts:50-86`, `:100-143`, `:148-182`). Functionally this works, but it drifts from the tech design's cached/bounded projection model for long-running processes.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.1\",\"AC-7.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"The 2-second performance NFR for turn/archive reads at 5,000 archive entries was not measured against a real Convex-backed runtime during this review.\",\"Manual end-to-end verification with `pnpm run convex:dev` and `pnpm dev` was not performed; production-path conclusions are based on code inspection plus automated test results.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}"}}
